1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,809
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:06,000
In this lesson, we will put the
right resgrid app on each device.

3
00:00:06,409 --> 00:00:09,880
A configured department still
needs members and shared devices to

4
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:13,060
sign in to the correct department
with the correct permissions.

5
00:00:13,439 --> 00:00:16,579
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,579 --> 00:00:18,479
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:23,619
Members install the Responder app, a
tablet in Engine 1 runs the Unit app and

8
00:00:23,619 --> 00:00:25,579
a station screen shows the Big Board.

9
00:00:26,099 --> 00:00:28,700
Most members use Rez grid
through the Responder app.

10
00:00:29,139 --> 00:00:33,160
Getting everyone installed and signed
in is what lets dispatches reach them.

11
00:00:33,679 --> 00:00:37,090
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:37,090 --> 00:00:39,330
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:40,860
Responder application.

14
00:00:41,329 --> 00:00:45,539
The member app for receiving dispatches,
responding and setting status.

15
00:00:45,989 --> 00:00:50,820
Have every member install the Responder
app, sign in and allow notifications.

16
00:00:50,999 --> 00:00:52,070
Unit application.

17
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:55,420
The in-vehicle app that
represents an apparatus.

18
00:00:55,809 --> 00:01:00,109
Install the Unit app on each
apparatus tablet and select its unit.

19
00:01:00,279 --> 00:01:01,580
Dispatch application.

20
00:01:01,999 --> 00:01:04,970
The dispatcher view for
creating and managing calls.

21
00:01:05,359 --> 00:01:09,580
Give dispatch access to the people
who dispatch, then have them sign in.

22
00:01:09,949 --> 00:01:11,939
Incident command and accountability.

23
00:01:12,550 --> 00:01:15,880
Incident command and accountability
for incident commanders.

24
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:19,699
Give command access to the
officers who run incidents.

25
00:01:19,869 --> 00:01:20,529
Big Board.

26
00:01:20,989 --> 00:01:24,169
A station display of
calls, units and personnel.

27
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:28,129
Open the Big Board on a station
screen and choose what it shows.

28
00:01:28,349 --> 00:01:28,980
Dashboard.

29
00:01:29,469 --> 00:01:33,609
The department home page: current
status, staffing and activity.

30
00:01:34,019 --> 00:01:37,399
Decide which devices each role
will use and share the app

31
00:01:37,399 --> 00:01:39,000
download links with your members.

32
00:01:39,149 --> 00:01:40,059
My Profile.

33
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:44,409
Your own profile, contact details
and notification preferences.

34
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:48,140
Decide which devices each role
will use and share the app

35
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:49,699
download links with your members.

36
00:01:49,919 --> 00:01:50,899
Your Departments.

37
00:01:51,310 --> 00:01:53,339
Switch between the
departments you belong to.

38
00:01:53,879 --> 00:01:57,320
Decide which devices each role
will use and share the app

39
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,909
download links with your members.

40
00:01:59,099 --> 00:02:01,799
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

41
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:02,809
Step 1.

42
00:02:03,369 --> 00:02:07,039
Set up a member device with Responder
and notification permissions.

43
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:08,189
Step 2.

44
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:12,010
Set up an apparatus tablet
with Unit and select its unit.

45
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:13,140
Step 3.

46
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:18,130
Grant appropriate Dispatch or Command
access and configure a station Big Board.

47
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:19,780
Now verify the result.

48
00:02:20,299 --> 00:02:23,519
Check the active department,
device identity, and a

49
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,160
controlled notification test.

50
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:28,000
Check what a shared
station screen exposes.

51
00:02:28,519 --> 00:02:33,280
A common problem to watch for: Installing
an app does not prove alerts arrive.

52
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:38,260
Verify OS notification and location
settings on the actual device used.

53
00:02:38,539 --> 00:02:40,109
Your practice task is simple.

54
00:02:40,509 --> 00:02:44,990
Use a sample member, unit tablet,
dispatcher, and station display to

55
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:46,809
follow the same training incident.

56
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,509
Record which devices complete the test.

57
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:53,820
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

58
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:57,549
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
